{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"153787d8cbad05908f2ba437558e96c2d5d09a4d6cb7be7e79ccccebf34604ba","digest":{"component_or_area":"close precheck gate","key_entities":["src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py","_check_work_landed","_referencing_commits","_check_file_impact_vs_diff","_union_file_impact","tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py::test_work_landed_skips_commit_discovery_when_scope_has_no_impact"],"problem_keywords":["performance","precheck","file impact","commit discovery","unnecessary work"],"propositions":["Closing a ticket with no file impact in the accepted ticket/descendant scope unconditionally invokes _referencing_commits, which scans full git history and resolves all historical ticket references.","The empty file-impact guard in _check_file_impact_vs_diff already exists but runs after the expensive commit discovery, causing unnecessary work.","Moving the file-impact union check before _referencing_commits eliminates the performance regression for no-impact closes without affecting impact-present, descendant-credit, or administrative-disposition enforcement.","A regression test must fail if the unconditional commit discovery is reintroduced on the empty-impact path."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787566027267152001,"uuid":"a57f25c5-f81c-4a69-8569-2c691383ef2c"}